Reverse String (Two-Pointer Approach)
This method reverses a character array in-place using the two-pointer technique.
One pointer starts at the beginning and the other at the end of the array. Characters are swapped while moving both pointers toward the center.
The solution handles edge cases like null input and does not use any extra data structures.
Time Complexity: O(n) — each character is visited once
Space Complexity: O(1) — reversal is done in-place without extra memory
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public void reverseString(char[] s) {
        if(s==null) return;
       int i=0;
       int j=s.length-1;
       while(i<j){
        char temp=s[i];
        s[i]=s[j];
        s[j]=temp;
        i++;
        j--;
       }
        
    }
}
